    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build passes with all 59 tests green, including `Cp47Tests` (the new holiday-business-day test) and `Cp20Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI extended the business-day rule for the registration date to cover public holidays in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **Added a public-holiday calendar** (`PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS`) \u2014 an immutable `Set<LocalDate>` with the five fixed dates: 2026-01-01, 2026-01-26, 2026-04-25, 2026-12-25, 2026-12-28.\n\n2. **Rewrote `toBusinessDay(...)`** from a single weekend-shift switch into a loop that advances the date one day at a time while it's a weekend *or* a listed holiday, returning the first non-holiday weekday. This correctly handles chained cases \u2014 e.g. a holiday landing right after a weekend, consecutive holidays, or a holiday that itself falls on a weekend (like 2026-04-25, a Saturday). Extracted the weekend check into a small `isWeekend` helper for readability.\n\nThe existing behavior for plain weekdays and weekends is preserved; the only new effect is rolling forward past holidays. All 59 tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
